whats an ip?


==>     whats an IP address?
internet protocol address
for a device to communicate with any other device, it needs an IP address

every IPv4 address comes in this format:
a.b.c.d

A, B, C, D are called octal!
the value of each octal go from 0 to 255



==>     rules of and roles of IP addresses:
tho we cant use all the address within this range of 0-255.0-255.0-255.0-255
some addresses are resolved to 

1- NETWORK ADDRESS ID: 
The very first IP in a subnet range (where all host bits are 0). It identifies the network itself.
        Example: In 192.168.1.0/24, 192.168.1.0 is the network address.

2- BROADCAST ADDRESS:
the very last IP address in a subnet range
192.168.1.255
    this is used to send data to every device on that network segment


3- Usable Host Addresses:
the only IP address between ID and BROADCAST: that can be assigned to devices


